          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How many circular arrangements of the word ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DECIMALS",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " are there if",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7!=5040$",
          "worked": "There are eight distinct letters.\n\n$$N=(8-1)!=7!=5040.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "D, C, M and L are together?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4!\\times4!=576$",
          "worked": "Treat D, C, M and L as one block. Together with E, I, A and S, there are five entities, giving $4!$ circular arrangements. The four letters inside the block have $4!$ arrangements.\n\n$$N=4!\\times4!=576.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "D, E, C are together, and L, S are also together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4!\\times3!\\times2!=288$",
          "worked": "Treat D, E, C as one block and L, S as another. These two blocks and I, M, A give five entities, with $4!$ circular arrangements. The blocks have $3!$ and $2!$ internal arrangements.\n\n$$N=4!\\times3!\\times2!=288.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q15-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the vowels are separate?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4!\\times5\\times4\\times3=1440$.\n\nPlace E, I and A in distinct gaps between the consonants.",
          "worked": "Arrange the five consonants D, C, M, L and S circularly in $4!$ ways. Their five gaps allow the three distinct vowels E, I and A to be placed in $5\\times4\\times3$ ways, with no two vowels adjacent.\n\n$$N=4!\\times5\\times4\\times3=1440.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q15-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "M, A and S are together but D, E are separate?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3!\\times3!\\times4\\times3=432$.\n\nArrange the M/A/S block with I, C and L, then place D and E in distinct gaps.",
          "worked": "Treat M, A and S as one block. Arrange this block with I, C and L circularly in $3!$ ways. Place D and E in two different gaps among the four gaps in $4\\times3$ ways. The M/A/S block has $3!$ internal arrangements.\n\n$$N=3!\\times4\\times3\\times3!=432.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
